{"name": "Campus Point Coffee", "address": "6560 Pardall Rd", "city": "Goleta", "state": "CA", "categories": "Food, Cafes, Coffee & Tea, Bakeries, Restaurants", "hours": null, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": false, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "free", "RestaurantsTakeOut": null, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "Music": null, "Ambience": null}, "business_stars": 4.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2020-01-10 17:12:03", "review_text": "A friend got me interested in this coffee shop when she mentioned they sell vegan cookies. I'm vegan, and it's actually rather tough to find vegan sweet snacks in IV, so I was excited to try Campus Point. Funnily enough, when I headed over for a studying session, they were sold out! Guess those cookies must be good. 

However, the coconut charcoal mocha I tried was delicious--and vegan! Staff were super friendly, and I appreciated the indoor and outdoor seating options. Also, there's a toilet, which is a bonus, and the empanadas looked really yummy. I'll have to try one next time I visit."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2020-01-08 22:10:42", "review_text": "Finally a place in Isla Vista with a bathroom!

Beyond the much needed bathroom this cafe offers a plethora of interesting drinks on top of providing all the basics. I got an iced charcoal mocha that was perfect to get rid of my mid afternoon slump."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2020-01-08 06:06:23", "review_text": "This is such a cute lil coffee shop in the heart of IV. There's tables inside and outside to do work or chill, and sometimes there's an open mic outside. Prices are average for your local non-corporate coffee shop. The menu has a wide variety of drinks, and sometimes they post about BOGO's or 50% off on their instagram page. I'd definitely recommend this place to anyone who loves coffee and needs a place to study!"}]}

{"name": "Javan's", "address": "938 Embarcadero Del Nrte", "city": "Goleta", "state": "CA", "categories": "Sandwiches, Restaurants, Burgers", "hours": null, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "free", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"romantic": false, "intimate": false, "touristy": false, "hipster": false, "divey": false, "classy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-02-25 06:54:05", "review_text": "Sigh ... Javan's is no more :'(  I miss it already."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2013-09-10 00:43:52", "review_text": "It perplexes me that this place is always so empty. Honestly it is the best food in IV without a doubt and it's because the owners double as the cooks and are invested in the overall quality of their ingredients and product. They are always entertaining and you could learn a thing or two from just conversing with them during your lunch. Consider helping out this humble mom and pop shop before heading to a big franchise restaurant because they do not compromise anything in their menu and are competitively priced compared to the rest of IV. 

I would recommend the Tuna sandwich for it's delicious combination of dressings and tastiness of the fish. Every bite is savory and leaves you wanting more. You can't go wrong with any of the sandwiches really though."}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2013-09-09 04:07:36", "review_text": "The owners of this place should seriously consider investing in a good quality sign for out front.  Currently they have an unlit vinyl sign so the place is basically unnoticeable, especially at night.  I bet they would really see business improve if they weren't cheap about the sign.

Good sandwiches and chili though."}]}

{"name": "Minnow Cafe", "address": "9 Breakwater", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Restaurants, Delis", "hours": null, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": false, "validated": false, "lot": true, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "no", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": false, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"touristy": false, "hipster": false, "romantic": false, "divey": false, "intimate": false, "trendy": false, "classy": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2011-08-11 16:25:16", "review_text": "This place is perfect to get some seafood in Santa Barbara! I was glad to be able to find this hole in a wall while walking with my group for lunch. 

I ordered the clam chowder bread bowl and fish and chips. Clam chowder was very delicious and fresh. The fish was crispy and made into perfection. 

The best part is that you can order the food right away and simply sit at the tables outside to eat near the harbor where the ocean is so close. So if you want to get food in a quickly manner in order to have more time to explore the other areas in Santa Barbara, I would highly recommend Minnow Cafe."}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2011-04-08 00:39:53", "review_text": "Hard to beat for a fast-food-type breakfast or lunch at the marina. Simple, good food, well prepared."}, {"review_stars": 3.0, "review_date": "2011-03-20 03:51:33", "review_text": "I really like the Minnow...I mean you can't beat the location for a fast food establishment and the Fish Tacos are pretty good...BUT I'm always horrified to discover how much this fast food experience costs.  I mean, it's really not very good food unless you view it as cheap (but it's not).  Great thing, sitting outside by the harbor watching the BPs go by while you eat cheap (seeming) food.  Bad part, greasy spoon food served on paper plates by snarky staff with condiments that blow away...but it ain't cheap.  Guess that's Santa Barbara."}]}

{"name": "Montecito Confections", "address": "1150 Coast Village Rd, Ste E", "city": "Montecito", "state": "CA", "categories": "Restaurants, Bakeries, Food", "hours": {"Monday": "9:0-17:0", "Tuesday": "9:0-17:0", "Wednesday": "9:0-17:0", "Thursday": "9:0-17:0", "Friday": "9:0-17:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": null, "OutdoorSeating": null, "WiFi": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": null, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "Music": null, "Ambience": null}, "business_stars": 4.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-08-14 04:36:40", "review_text": "Ordered a white cake with buttercream. When I placed the order they suggested a light lemon cream filling which I went with. It was beyond perfect. Light fluffy buttercream, moist cake, and the filling was a perfect match up. Yep, I will be back!"}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-08-07 19:34:34", "review_text": "Katie baked the wedding cake of my dreams. It came out exactly as I wanted and was delicious. We had three tiers: two were red velvet and one was vanilla custard cake with fresh raspberries. I am very happy with our decision to choose her."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-05-09 15:00:38", "review_text": "Katie Teall is an ANGEL!!!  I made a wedding cake for the daughter of a very close High School friend and the Fondant I bought (FondArt) was horrible.  I spent about 7 hours kneading it and rolling it, and no matter what I did when I covered a tier of the cake it cracked.  I was so stressed that decided to go to Montecito Confections to see if I could buy Fondant there.  I got there and asked Katie Teall the sweet adorable, British owner if she could help me.  she explained that she sold the store and the rest of her Fondant was for the last 15 wedding cakes that she had to deliver during the summer.  She must have seen my face of stress, exhaustion, just lost, and asked:  How big is your cake?  I told her and she said:  Do you want me to cover it in Fondant for you?  I jumped to hug her and kiss her and hug her and kissed her some more.

I came home and the mother of the bride carried the bottom tier and we went back to Montecito Confections to be saved by Katie.  We arrived and she said where is the rest of the cake?  I did not want to take advantage so we just took the biggest tier.  She said:  Bring it!

Home we went after hugging Katie and kissing her some more and got help and left with two more tiers.  Katie my angel covered the three tiers!!! She was my angel.  The mother of the bride broke in tears, I guess she was worried that I was never going to serve the wedding cake.  These were tears of relief!  We ended up having the most beautiful cake and thanks to Katie.  Katie also build the cake, putting all three tiers together.  Then explained to me how to decorate it.  She told me to get a photo of the container of her fondant because she had tried all the different brands and that was the best of them all.  She said that mine was impossible to work with since it was too dry!  Katie is a walking ANGEL.  I love her, love her and love her.  All the kisses and hugs are not enough to thank her for saving the wedding cake and so much more."}]}

{"name": "El Taco Tequila Taqueria", "address": "14 E Cota St", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Restaurants, Mexican", "hours": null, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "no", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"romantic": false, "intimate": false, "touristy": false, "hipster": false, "divey": false, "classy": false, "trendy": true, "upscale": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 3.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 2.0, "review_date": "2013-12-06 03:03:14", "review_text": "On Thursday night I went to this place after a concert. A few friends and I wanted a bite and a drink. We ordered with a young woman who quickly told us they did not accommodate gluten free customers, even if you wanted a taco or tostada without the bread. Fine. I'll work around that I understand. We waited 20 minutes for our food, granted there was only one guy in the kitchen. We finally got our tacos and were missing one chicken taco and our guacamole. We ask the chef for the rest of our order and he says they are closing the kitchen. I go to the woman and tell her that we didn't get all our food and she tells me I'm lying. I point to the plates on our table to show her we didn't. I ask for our money back and she declines. We end up getting into a fight about one chicken taco and guac. 

I have worked in restaurants before and I would never scold a customer over a $3 taco. I even offed to pay for it and she wouldn't let me. Really terrible customer service. The chef did make us some guac bc I think he felt bad that we were hungry and upset. By that point we had eaten what we were served and didn't have anything to put it on.

That being said the food we get was yummy. Too bad our experience ended on such a bad note."}, {"review_stars": 1.0, "review_date": "2013-03-28 15:50:04", "review_text": "We both got food poisoning here - that lasted a whole day. We narrowed it down to either the chips & salsa, the queso app, or the carnitas tacos since that's the only thing BOTH of us ate. The food seemed great, but it seems to be all about pushing the drinks for $$ and food safety was left to the sidelines."}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2012-11-03 03:56:19", "review_text": "Great food. WOnderful atmosphere. Great Happy hour two for one Margaritas. I love the decor too. Beautiful Bar. Amazing flan!"}]}
